<title>HONG KONG: HK Nov orders on hand fall five pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Nov orders on hand fall five pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department on Monday said Hong Kong's November orders on hand fell five percent in value on the year against a six percent drop in October.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders on hand in November 1996 over November 1995 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						   Nov 1996   Oct 1996</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey    -5	   -6</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				 +1	   -1*</p>
<p> Textiles					  +1	   ***</p>
<p> Electronic Products			   -11	  -11*</p>
<p> Electrical products			   ***	  -3</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		   +9	   +5</p>
<p> Plastic products				-11	  -10</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		     -16	  -14</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
